Day 242/250: Minimum Pair Removal to Sort Array I

Problem Statement #3507

Problem Statement Explantion:

You are given an integer array nums. You can perform the following operation any number of times:

Find the adjacent pair of elements (nums[i],nums[i+1]) such that their sum is the minimum among all adjacent pairs.
If there is a tie (multiple pairs have the same minimum sum), choose the leftmost one.
Replace the pair with their sum, reducing the array length by 1.
Return the minimum number of operations needed to make the array non-decreasing (nums[i]≤nums[i+1] for all i).

Solution Approach:

Since the constraints for this problem are relatively small (N≤50), a greedy simulation is the most straightforward and efficient approach.

Key Logic:
Check Condition: First, we check if the array is already non-decreasing. If it is, we return 0.
Find Minimum Sum: In each step, we iterate through the current list to find the pair (i,i+1) that yields the smallest sum.
Tie-breaking: By iterating from left to right and only updating our "min index" if we find a sum strictly smaller than the current minimum, we naturally satisfy the "leftmost" requirement.
Transformation: We replace the two elements with their sum using a dynamic list structure (like ArrayList) and increment our operation counter.
Repeat: This continues until the non-decreasing condition is met.

Here's the code:

import java.util.*;

class Solution {
    public int minimumPairRemoval(int[] nums) {
        List<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int num : nums) {
            list.add(num);
        }

        int operations = 0;

        while (!isNonDecreasing(list)) {
            int minIdx = 0;
            long minSum = (long) list.get(0) + list.get(1);

            for (int i = 1; i < list.size() - 1; i++) {
                long currentSum = (long) list.get(i) + list.get(i + 1);
                if (currentSum < minSum) {
                    minSum = currentSum;
                    minIdx = i;
                }
            }

            list.set(minIdx, (int) minSum);
            list.remove(minIdx + 1);
            operations++;
        }

        return operations;
    }

    private boolean isNonDecreasing(List<Integer> list) {
        for (int i = 0; i < list.size() - 1; i++) {
            if (list.get(i) > list.get(i + 1)) {
                return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
}

Complexity:

Time Compelxity: O(N3)
Space Complexity: O(N)



